# Copyrighted visual reference — never commit
/reference/
*.reference.jpg
*.reference.png
__pycache__/
tools/figure-pipeline/.cache/

# The figure bakes USED to be ignored here as build output. They are committed through git-LFS now,
# and the reason is the whole point of the runtime API: an embedder cannot run headless Blender, so
# "regenerable" is true for this machine and useless to anyone else. A clone with no body cannot
# call Avatar.create(). See .gitattributes.

# Capture output — regenerable, large. Keep the tool, not the artifacts.
#
# ⚠️ THE PATTERN IS `/captures/**` AND NOT `/captures/`, AND THE DIFFERENCE IS LOAD-BEARING.
# Git will not descend into an EXCLUDED DIRECTORY, so a `!` negation inside one is never evaluated
# — "it is not possible to re-include a file if a parent directory of that file is excluded".
# Excluding the CONTENTS instead leaves the directory walkable and makes the exceptions below work.
# This was tried the wrong way round first and `git add` refused, which is how it was caught.
/captures/**

# ...EXCEPT the round's EVIDENCE, which is neither large nor reliably regenerable.
#
# 🔴 R31 found that every plate, table, manifest, blind key and crop backing a round's claims lives
# under an ignored path with no history and no protection from another agent's `git clean` — the
# round that discovered it had its entire evidentiary basis there. A capture is regenerable in
# principle; the SESSION is not. Timings depend on machine load, a blind key is generated once, and
# a manifest records what the live page actually was rather than what a URL claimed.
#
# So the DATA is kept (500 KB for R31) and the PLATES stay ignored (36 MB for the same round) —
# re-excluded below, after the re-inclusion, because later rules win.
#
# Scoped to `hair-r31-*` deliberately rather than to all 242 capture directories: widening it is the
# owner's call and not an agent's, and the narrow form is trivially reversible.
!/captures/hair-r31-*/
!/captures/hair-r31-*/**
/captures/hair-r31-*/**/*.png
/captures/hair-r31-*/**/*.jpg
/captures/hair-r31-*/**/*.jpeg

# R32, same rule and same reason. REQ-064's refutation rests on a gated 236,792-pixel mask and a
# fourteen-arm sweep; the PLATES regenerate from `tools/critic/hair-glint.mjs --masks --arms`, the
# REPORT is the thing a reader needs beside the claim.
!/captures/hair-r32-*/
!/captures/hair-r32-*/**
/captures/hair-r32-*/**/*.png
/captures/hair-r32-*/**/*.jpg
/captures/hair-r32-*/**/*.jpeg

# R33, REQ-063's registered round. Same rule: the report and the write-up are what a reader needs
# beside the claim; the eleven plates regenerate from `hair-rimshadow.mjs --masks --arms --dim`.
!/captures/hair-r33-*/
!/captures/hair-r33-*/**
/captures/hair-r33-*/**/*.png
/captures/hair-r33-*/**/*.jpg
/captures/hair-r33-*/**/*.jpeg

# 🔴 AND NEVER THE ANSWER KEY TO A BLIND PANEL, WHICH THE RULE ABOVE ALMOST COMMITTED.
# `captures/hair-r31-separation/blind-KEY.json` is the mapping for a three-arm blind that HAS NOT
# BEEN RUN. Tracking it would put the key inside the tree every judge subagent can read — the exact
# defect `blind_ab.mjs` carried until it was repaired this same day, arriving by a completely
# different route. A structural guard only protects the path it is on: that fix lives in the tool,
# and this key was not written by that tool.
*blind-KEY.json
*.key.json
/captures/**/blind/
